{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMA5E6M1F3cqcQv46bdT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VDnbZfyPwvSGdPFC14rMP2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"L=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-1\nnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs --registry-path \"$L/deep-review-findings-registry.json\" --state-log \"$L/deep-review-state.jsonl\"; echo EXIT=$?\npython3 -c \"import json;r=json.load(open('$L/deep-review-findings-registry.json'));print(r.get('dimensionCoverage'))\"\nsed -n 2299,2370p .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | cut -c1-500","description":"Derive verdict and read report spec"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4332,"cache_read_input_tokens":257963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4332},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:55:17.803Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VDnbZfyPwvSGdPFC14rMP2":{"command":"L=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-1\nnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs --registry-path \"$L/deep-review-findings-registry.json\" --state-log \"$L/deep-review-state.jsonl\"; echo EXIT=$?\npython3 -c \"import json;r=json.load(open('$L/deep-review-findings-registry.json'));print(r.get('dimensionCoverage'))\"\nsed -n 2299,2370p .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | cut -c1-500","description":"Derive verdict and read report spec"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VDnbZfyPwvSGdPFC14rMP2","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"status\":\"ok\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"has_advisories\":true,\"active_p0\":0,\"active_p1\":0,\"active_p2\":3,\"search_debt\":0,\"failed_required_gate_ids\":[]}\nEXIT=0\n{'correctness': True, 'security': True, 'traceability': True, 'maintainability': True}\n      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        instructions: |\n          **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n             - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n             - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n             - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n             - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n             - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n             - When {state_paths.findings_registry} carries a `frontier` object, list every node in `frontier.nodes` whose status is `exhausted` or `blocked` as follow-up review work: its nodeId, status, reason, scope, and `nextDimension` (or \"every dimension reviewed\" when it is null). These are the nodes a review dashboard lists as `Follow-up` lines in `## 10B. FRONTIER`; on a fan-out root, each lineage's dashboard lists its own, and the merged node ids carry the lineage label. They do not cha\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: a `completed-continue` extension keeps the prior review report as `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. See `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n\n      step_derive_release_readiness_state:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:55:20.193Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"status\":\"ok\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"has_advisories\":true,\"active_p0\":0,\"active_p1\":0,\"active_p2\":3,\"search_debt\":0,\"failed_required_gate_ids\":[]}\nEXIT=0\n{'correctness': True, 'security': True, 'traceability': True, 'maintainability': True}\n      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        instructions: |\n          **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n             - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n             - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n             - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n             - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n             - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n             - When {state_paths.findings_registry} carries a `frontier` object, list every node in `frontier.nodes` whose status is `exhausted` or `blocked` as follow-up review work: its nodeId, status, reason, scope, and `nextDimension` (or \"every dimension reviewed\" when it is null). These are the nodes a review dashboard lists as `Follow-up` lines in `## 10B. FRONTIER`; on a fan-out root, each lineage's dashboard lists its own, and the merged node ids carry the lineage label. They do not cha\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: a `completed-continue` extension keeps the prior review report as `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. See `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n\n      step_derive_release_readiness_state:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-3/review-report.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":71,"lines":["+---","+title: \"Deep Review Report: 012 deep-loop command offers (lineage opus-medium-3)\"","+description: \"Five-iteration review of the deep-loop offer gate, its Python fallback and the packet 013 typed-command hint. One P1, nine P2, verdict FAIL on the coverage gate.\"","+---","+","+# Deep Review Report: 012 deep-loop command offers (lineage opus-medium-3)","+","+## 1. Executive Summary","+","+- **Verdict: FAIL.** `review-verdict.cjs` derives it. The findings alone give CONDITIONAL: no P0 and one active P1. The coverage gate also fails with `traceability-incomplete`, because both core protocols, `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence`, ended `partial` on the gaps below. That failed gate forces FAIL.","+- Active findings: P0 0, P1 1, P2 9. Every finding cites a file and line in the declared scope, and the evidence and scope gates pass.","+- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (5 of 5, stopPolicy `max-iterations`). All four dimensions were covered.","+- Release readiness: `in-progress`.","+- Review focus: the deep-loop offer gate in `command-attach.ts`, the Python fallback in `skill_advisor.py`, and the packet 013 typed-command hint. Every iteration probed the TypeScript source directly, using node type stripping. The Python module was imported read-only and its CLI was never run.","+","+## 2. Planning Trigger","+","+The P1 blocks a PASS. Route it to `/speckit:plan` for packet 012 or a follow-up child. Before any code changes, the operator has to decide one thing: when a stuck-run complaint also types `/deep:review`, should the brief offer the typed command (what the native path does today) or the doctor (what the Python path and the packet docs say)?","+","+## 3. Active Finding Registry","+","+| ID | Sev | Dim | Title | Location |","+|----|-----|-----|-------|----------|","+| O3-R3-P1-006 | P1 | traceability | A typed `/deep:review` in a stuck-run complaint still reaches the native brief while the Python gate drops it. AC-027 records both as withheld | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:434` |","+| O3-R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | A typed deep command is lost when the prompt also types a longer, different command (TS longest-key rule; Python disagrees) | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:238` |","+| O3-R1-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | The degraded path drops `typed`, so a typed deep command still gets the A/B/C offer (013 REQ-006) | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:250` |","+| O3-R2-P2-003 | P2 | security | `skip`, `avoid`, `instead of` and `refuse` do not withhold the deep command, in TS or Python | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:440` |","+| O3-R2-P2-004 | P2 | security | A stuck-run complaint attaches the run-policy doctor despite \"please don't run anything\" | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:837` |","+| O3-R2-P2-005 | P2 | security | The Python `_has_loop_ask` is quadratic: a 96 000-char prompt takes 6.3 s against a 3 s fallback timeout | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:4718` |","+| O3-R3-P2-007 | P2 | traceability | AC-008's evidence text says \"accepted that as Met\" while its status is Waived | `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/acceptance-criteria.md:65` |","+| O3-R4-P2-008 | P2 | maintainability | Python inlines the vocabulary lists that TS keeps as data, and nothing generates or compares them | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:4529` |","+| O3-R5-P2-009 | P2 | correctness | The review mode cue misses `checking`/`inspecting`/`scanning`, though its comment says the -ing form counts | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:384` |","+| O3-R5-P2-010 | P2 | correctness | The stage-one loop rule reads raw loop wording without the gate's subject and refusal exceptions (inference, not scorer-run) | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:449` |","+","+## 4. Remediation Workstreams","+","+1. **Typed-command parity (P1-006, P2-001, P2-002).** Settle how a typed command interacts with the stuck-run rule. Make `typedCommandForTop` and the Python `_typed_deep_command` choose the same way: prefer the deep command the route attached, not the longest key across unrelated commands. Have `degradedRecommendations` set `typed: true` on rows it keeps because the prompt typed them. Extend `deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts` so the fixture's `typedReviewKept` is asserted through `attachTypedCommand` as well.","+2. **Refusal and consent vocabulary (P2-003, P2-004).** Add `skip`, `avoid`, `instead of` and `rather than` to `RUN_ASK_NEGATED` and its Python twin, as the typed-command decline list already does. Withhold the doctor when the prompt says not to run anything.","+3. **Fallback performance (P2-005).** Bound the Python scan, for example by checking the prefix tail only, since the patterns are end-anchored.","+4. **Sync cost and vocabulary (P2-008, P2-009, P2-010).** Use one vocabulary source for both languages. Add the -ing defect-check verbs. Let the stage-one rule reuse the gate's exceptions, or confirm by a scorer run that it does no harm.","+5. **Doc hygiene (P2-007).** Reword AC-008's evidence cell to match `Waived`.","+","+## 5. Spec Seed","+","+- REQ-020 should state end-to-end parity: what the native brief prints, after `attachTypedCommand`, equals what the Python gate keeps.","+- REQ-015 should either list the refusal verbs it covers or say outright that it covers only the six named prompts.","+","+## 6. Plan Seed","+","+- T1: decide the typed-plus-stuck rule. T2: implement it in both languages and in the degraded row mapper. T3: add fixture rows for every probe prompt quoted above. T4: widen the refusal and cue vocabularies. T5: fix the Python scan cost and add a timing test. T6: reword AC-008.","+","+## 7. Traceability Status","+","+| Protocol | Status | Notes |","+|----------|--------|-------|","+| spec_code | partial | REQ-020 fails end to end, REQ-015's general rule has gaps, and 013 REQ-006 fails on the degraded path. REQ-005 and 013 REQ-001 pass. |","+| checklist_evidence | partial | AC-027 overclaims, and AC-008's text contradicts its status. The other AC rows cite concrete evidence. Probes and suites were not rerun, because this lineage may not run repo tooling. |","+| overlays | not run | skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code and playbook_capability were not exercised. |","+","+## 8. Deferred Items","+","+- Run the full scorer on \"several passes of the linter failed, review the config\" to confirm or drop P2-010.","+- Run `skill_advisor.py --stdin` on the typed prompts to confirm what the degraded brief prints for P2-002. Today that rests on reading `skill-advisor-cli.ts:1501-1510`.","+","+## 9. Audit Appendix","+","+- Iterations: 001 correctness, 002 security, 003 traceability, 004 maintainability, 005 correctness (second pass).","+- newFindingsRatio by iteration: 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.29, 0.15.","+- Terminal gates: evidence pass, scope pass, coverage fail (`traceability-incomplete`).","+- Probe scripts (lineage scratch only): `scratch/probe.mts`, `scratch/redos.mts`.","+- steer.md was absent at every check."]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-3/review-report.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VDnbZfyPwvSGdPFC14rMP2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
