he accepted typed-on-stuck exception, or align the Python gate with the native hook\", \"findings\": [\"R1-P1-001\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"WS-2\", \"title\": \"Make commandOnlyMentioned linear in the occurrence count (TS and Python)\", \"findings\": [\"R2-P2-001\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"WS-3\", \"title\": \"Extend the parity guard to the inline regex vocabulary\", \"findings\": [\"R4-P2-001\"]}","+  ],","+  \"specSeed\": [\"Amend REQ-020 and SC-005 to name the typed-on-stuck exception the operator accepted\", \"Decide whether the Python fallback should keep the typed run row on a stuck prompt to match the native hook\"],","+  \"planSeed\": [\"Add an attachTypedCommand-level test for the typed-stuck fixture case\", \"Hoist the per-occurrence RegExp construction out of the occurrence loop\", \"Add fixture cases for every COUNT_WORDS entry and the inline symptom/artifact words\"],","+  \"findingClasses\": [\"spec/evidence drift on accepted exception\", \"bounded algorithmic complexity\", \"incomplete parity guard\"],","+  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/spec.md\", \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/acceptance-criteria.md\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/fixtures/deep-loop-offer-cases.json\"],","+  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false","+}","+```","+","+## 3. Active Finding Registry","+","+| ID | Sev | Dimension | file:line | Title |","+|----|-----|-----------|-----------|-------|","+| R1-P1-001 | P2 (was P1) | correctness → traceability | `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/acceptance-criteria.md:1`; origin `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:428` | The typed-on-stuck exception is accepted in prose, but REQ-020, SC-005 and AC-027 still state parity, and the hook output contradicts them |","+| R2-P2-001 | P2 | security | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:784` | commandOnlyMentioned rescans the whole prefix for every occurrence, so cost grows with the square of the repeat count (bounded by the 10K cap) |","+| R4-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts:72` | The drift guard checks only the three exported phrase lists, so a one-sided edit to the inline regex vocabulary passes both suites |","+","+**R1-P1-001.** Evidence: `attachTypedCommand` (`advisor-recommend.ts:428-447`) runs after `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`:556-561`, `:628-633`) and replaces the doctor command that `attachCommand` returns for a stuck run (`command-attach.ts:837-841`). `typedCommandForTop` (`command-attach.ts:257-265`) has no stuck check. The Python gate drops the run row on a stuck prompt even when it is typed (`skill_advisor.py:4848-4853`). The packet's own hook capture prints `/deep:review (ask)` for \"my deep review run is stuck, /deep:review again\" (`scratch/probes/fresh-review-hook.txt:28`). Impact: the native and fallback advisors disagree on this prompt, while REQ-020 and SC-005 (`spec.md:218, 249`) and AC-027 say they agree. Fix: amend the requirement text to name the exception, or align the Python gate, and test the typed-stuck case at the `attachTypedCommand` layer. Disposition: open advisory. findingClass: spec/evidence drift on an accepted exception. scopeProof: the four refs above. affectedSurfaceHints: spec.md, acceptance-criteria.md, deep-loop-offer-cases.*, skill_advisor.py.","+","+**R2-P2-001.** Evidence: TS `'do not run /deep:review. '` repeated takes 10.5 ms at 5K chars, 506 ms at 20K and 1,517 ms at 80K. Python takes 349 ms at 10K. The 10K cap is at `advisor-tool-schemas.ts:257` and `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:233`. Impact: up to about 0.35 s of extra fallback latency for each deep run row checked on a hostile or pasted prompt. Fix: build the lead regexes once, and test each against a bounded tail window instead of the full prefix. findingClass: bounded algorithmic complexity. affectedSurfaceHints: command-attach.ts commandOnlyMentioned, skill_advisor.py _deep_command_only_mentioned.","+","+**R4-P2-001.** Evidence: the guard at `deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts:72` iterates `LOOP_WORDING`, `LOOP_NAMES` and `LOOP_WANT_LEADS` only. `COUNT_WORDS` (`command-attach.ts:335`) is mirrored inline at `skill_advisor.py:4490`, and no fixture case uses thirty, forty, fifty or dozen. Impact: a one-sided vocabulary edit passes both suites. Fix: export the inline word lists, or add a fixture case per entry. findingClass: incomplete parity guard.","+","+## 4. Remediation Workstreams","+- **P0:** none.","+- **P1:** none.","+- **P2 advisories:** WS-1 (R1-P1-001), WS-2 (R2-P2-001), WS-3 (R4-P2-001), as listed in the Planning Packet.","+","+## 5. Spec Seed","+- REQ-020: add \"except a typed command on a stuck run, where the native hook keeps the typed command (operator decision 2026-11-23)\", or require the Python gate to match.","+- SC-005: exclude that prompt from \"gives its stated result through the prompt hook\", or restate its stated result as `/deep:review (ask)`.","+","+## 6. Plan Seed","+1. Add a vitest case that sends the `typed-stuck` fixture prompt through `attachTypedCommand` and pins the accepted result.","+2. Decide on Python parity for typed-on-stuck, then update `_apply_deep_loop_offer_gate` and the fixture's `typedReviewKept` semantics to match.","+3. Refactor `commandOnlyMentioned` and its Python copy so the per-occurrence work is independent of prefix length, with a timing assertion at the 10K cap.","+4. Add fixture run cases for each COUNT_WORDS entry, or export the list and extend the guard loop.","+","+## 7. Traceability Status","+","+### Core Protocols","+| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Drift |","+|----------|--------|----------|-------|","+| spec_code | partial | Loop-ask clauses map to `command-attach.ts:277-640`. The deferred mode cue is at `:899-924`. The stage-one rule at `explicit.ts:449-460` scores no depth word. | REQ-020 holds at the `attachCommand` layer, not at the hook (R1-P1-001) |","+| checklist_evidence | partial | The AC rows cite observed evidence. | AC-027 is verified on a narrower layer than SC-005 requires |","+","+### Overlay Protocols","+| Protocol | Status | Notes |","+|----------|--------|-------|","+| skill_agent | notApplicable | No skill-agent contract in scope |","+| agent_cross_runtime | notApplicable | No agent files in scope |","+| feature_catalog_code | notApplicable | No feature catalog in scope |","+| playbook_capability | notApplicable | No manual testing playbook in scope |","+","+- **AC_COVERAGE:** exempt for this lineage. The packet uses `acceptance-criteria.md` rather than `checklist.md`, so the signal does not apply. All 29 AC rows read Met or Waived (AC-008 waived with ADR-003).","+","+## 8. Deferred Items","+- Routed path and named loop mode: `attachCommand` on a routed single mode does not consult `NAMED_LOOP_MODE`, so a router that picks review for \"run 5 research iterations on review tooling\" would offer `/deep:review`. I did not run the compiled router, so this is unverified.","+- `overnight` and `convergence` beside \"research\" lift the hub at stage one (`explicit.ts:451`) though neither is in the spec's explicit-loop list. The offer gate still withholds the command.","+- Known word-rule misses that the packet already documents (`implementation-summary.md:239`): \"Skip the deep review on this branch\", \"multi-pass compiler design review\".","+","+## Dimension Expansion Map","+- Saturated directions: none recorded by the reducer.","+- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.","+- Selected directions: correctness (iterations 1 and 5), security (2), traceability (3), maintainability (4).","+- Remaining frontier: compiled-router mode choice versus the prompt's named loop mode. Not probed, because dist is not built in this worktree.","+","+## 9. Search Ledger","+*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*","+","+## 10. Audit Appendix","+- **Convergence:** newFindingsRatio by iteration 1.0, 0.17, 0.08, 0.13, 0.0. The reducer's convergenceScore reached 1.0 at iteration 5. Stop reason: maxIterationsReached.","+- **Coverage:** 4 of 4 dimensions (`dimensionCoverage` all true).","+- **Ruled out:** catastrophic regex backtracking (linear on every probe shape), forging the `typed` flag from prompt text (`advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308`), injection into the brief head (sanitized known command keys), TS-vs-Python predicate drift (0 of 61 out-of-fixture prompts), and a depth word lifting the hub at stage one.","+- **Probe artifacts (inside this lineage):** `probes/gate-probe.mjs`, `probes/redos*.{mjs,py}`, `probes/diff.{mjs,py}`, `probes/prompts.json`, `probes/py-typed.py`, and `probes/ts-resolve.mjs` (a resolve hook that loads the TS source without a dist build).","+- **Sources reviewed:** see `iterations/iteration-001.md` to `iteration-005.md`, Files Reviewed."]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-1/probes/emit-rm.err","/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-1/resource-map.md","/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/review/lineages/opus-medium-1/review-report.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SwxC54g1ZVJmA5PHappTnA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
